productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Sabra Health Care REIT, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $5.4B market cap on $775M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 140% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.4010126199174893},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (SBRA) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/17/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_SBRA_Volatility_111326111602_1794586562.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586562.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What\u2019s Behind Sabra Health Care REIT (SBRA) Stock\u2019s Latest Move?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nasdaq-sbra/sabra-health-care-reit/news/whats-behind-sabra-health-care-reit-sbra-stocks-latest-move","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794291582.54,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.944,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sabra Health Care Director Michael J. Foster Sells 10,000 Shares at $20.98 Each","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/sabra-health-care-director-michael-j-foster-sells-10000-shares-at-2098-each","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794501834.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.66,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sabra Health Care REIT Director Michael J. Foster Announces Plan to Sell 10,000 